            <ArticleTitle>Primary care physicians and coronary heart disease prevention: a practice model.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>207-17</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary care physicians have an important role in coronary heart disease prevention. This paper discusses the results of a qualitative study conducted with Nova Scotian physicians to explore the following: physicians' expectations about their role in prevention; obstacles to providing preventive care; and, mechanisms by which preventive care occurs. The second part of the paper presents a practice model which is intended as a framework by which physicians may more effectively educate and counsel their patients about health issues, such as coronary heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
